⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of Verily Cooper
node C1 · C1 · ⟦Verily Cooper:C1:386c47⟧

WHO   — Verily Cooper — the knack of joining
WHAT  — The Joiner — a cooper whose hands make wood, argument, and people fit into seamless wholes, who lays down the trade of barrels to take up the trade of advocacy and becomes Alvin's friend and defender at the bar.
WHERE — C1 · Card  Framework inputs: The Tales of Alvin Maker  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because a thing rightly joined holds against any pressure; because a knack unexplained in a fearful land is a danger to its bearer, and Verily crossed an ocean to find where his gift belonged; because the law, like a barrel, only holds if its parts are made to fit.
HOW   — By the inward sense of how two things long to be one — feeling along the grain of wood, the grain of an argument, the grain of a divided company of people — and pressing them together until the seam disappears and the whole stands true.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  A cooper makes the staves fit so the water holds; a man of law makes the truth fit so the verdict holds — and Verily Cooper joins what was never meant to come apart.

